.godot/
*.tmp
builds/
build/

# Godot imports .glb models with "Extract Textures", which writes the embedded
# images out beside the model as loose .png/.jpg files. They are derived from
# the .glb — which already contains them — so committing them would duplicate
# tens of megabytes that are regenerated on first import anyway. Every real
# source asset in models/ is a .glb; anything else in there is generated.
#
# Do not delete these from a working tree without also clearing .godot/imported/
# for that model: Godot skips re-importing when the source .glb is unchanged,
# and the cached scene keeps a hard reference to the missing texture, which
# fails the model's load outright.
models/*.png
models/*.png.import
models/*.jpg
models/*.jpg.import
models/*.jpeg
models/*.jpeg.import
